# What the Vercel CLI uploads when deploying from the REPOSITORY ROOT.
#
# detomsite-frontend (Root Directory "frontend") and detomsite-student (Root
# Directory "frontend/student") must be deployed from the repo root, otherwise
# Vercel reports: The specified Root Directory "frontend" does not exist.
# That upload used to be ~143 MB, almost all of it Android sources and build
# outputs that no Vite build ever reads — this file cuts it to a few MB and
# makes those deploys much faster and less flaky.
#
# Patterns are anchored with a leading "/" (.gitignore semantics), so nothing
# inside frontend/ or backend/ is excluded by accident. Deploys that run from
# ./backend or ./frontend/<portal> do not read this file at all.

# Android app sources + Gradle intermediates (~89 MB). The APKs the sites
# actually publish live inside frontend/*/public and are deliberately kept.
/mobile/

# Ad-hoc APK copies at the repo root (the published ones are in frontend/).
/*.apk

# Deploy/inspection scratch output that was committed or left behind.
/verification/
/verification2/
/verify-final/
/*.js
/idx-*.html
/index-live.html
/fresh-index.html
/bundle-name.txt
/bundle-new-*
/*-login.json
/backend-deploy-check.txt
/backend/backend_commit.txt

# Local build output — Vercel runs the build itself.
/frontend/*/dist/
